---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
const lastUpdated = 'November 20, 2026';
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy" description={`Privacy Policy for ${SITE.name}: how client-side tool inputs, local storage, hosting logs, and Google AdSense advertising cookies are handled.`}>
  <article class="policy-card prose">
    <span class="badge badge-accent">Legal &amp; Transparency</span>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    <p class="lede">This Privacy Policy explains how {SITE.name} ({SITE.url}) handles information when you visit our website, use our browser-based DevOps tools, or read our technical guides.</p>

    <h2>1. Tool inputs and client-side processing</h2>
    <p>All developer and DevOps tools on {SITE.name} run 100% locally in your web browser using client-side JavaScript. When you paste Kubernetes manifests, Base64 strings, JWTs, logs, XML/JSON files, or environment variables into any tool or prompt redactor:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your pasted input is processed solely in your browser's local memory.</li>
      <li>{SITE.name} does <strong>not</strong> transmit, upload, log, or store your pasted tool inputs on any server.</li>
      <li>You can verify this behavior at any time using your browser's Network inspector or by auditing our open-source repository on <a href={SITE.repo} rel="noopener">GitHub</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>2. Local browser storage</h2>
    <p>To improve usability, {SITE.name} stores minimal preferences in your browser's <code>localStorage</code>, such as your light/dark theme choice (<code>theme</code>), cache-invalidation build identifier (<code>app_build_id</code>), and optional saved tool preferences prefixed with <code>opsmask:</code>. This data remains strictly on your device and can be cleared at any time through your browser settings.</p>

    <h2>3. Advertising and Google AdSense cookies</h2>
    <p>{SITE.name} uses <strong>Google AdSense</strong>, a third-party advertising service provided by Google LLC, to serve advertisements that help keep our tools free.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies (such as the DoubleClick cookie) to serve ads based on your prior visits to {SITE.name} or other websites on the internet.</li>
      <li>Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to you based on your visit to this site and/or other sites on the internet.</li>
      <li>You may opt out of personalized advertising at any time by visiting <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ads Settings</a>.</li>
      <li>Alternatively, you can opt out of a third-party vendor's use of cookies for personalized advertising by visiting <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">aboutads.info</a> or <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Your Online Choices (EU)</a>.</li>
      <li>For more information on how Google collects and processes data when you visit partner sites, please review <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Hosting and infrastructure access logs</h2>
    <p>{SITE.name} is hosted on Cloudflare Pages. Like standard web hosting providers, Cloudflare may temporarily process standard HTTP request metadata (such as IP address, user-agent, requested URL, and timestamp) at the network edge for DDoS mitigation, security filtering, and content delivery reliability. {SITE.name} does not receive personally identifiable user profiles from these logs.</p>

    <h2>5. External links</h2>
    <p>Our guides, cheatsheets, and footer contain links to external sites such as GitHub, Ko-fi, Kubernetes documentation, and RFC specifications. We are not responsible for the privacy practices or content of third-party websites.</p>

    <h2>6. Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>{SITE.name} is a technical resource intended for software developers and infrastructure engineers. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under the age of 13 (or the applicable age of digital consent in your jurisdiction).</p>

    <h2>7. Your privacy rights (GDPR &amp; CCPA)</h2>
    <p>Depending on your region (including the EEA, UK, and California), you may have rights regarding personal data processed by third-party advertising partners, including the right to opt out of personalized ads or withdraw cookie consent. You can manage browser cookies directly in your browser settings or use the Google Ads opt-out links listed in Section 3.</p>

    <h2>8. Changes to this policy &amp; contact</h2>
    <p>We may update this Privacy Policy as we add features or update third-party services. Any changes will be posted on this page with an updated revision date. If you have questions about this policy, please email us at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a> or visit our <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .policy-card {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-l);
    padding: 2rem 2.25rem;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
    max-width: 54rem;
  }
  .policy-card h1 {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.06rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .policy-card {
      padding: 1.35rem;
    }
  }
</style>
